The full route is built around the anchor, and `npm run build` succeeds (only console error anywhere is a missing `favicon.ico`).

**What's there now**

- **The anchor, untouched.** Full-bleed indigo canvas at yarn scale → the weave closes while an editorial frame draws in → held Chore Jacket with its name and price → the frame flies to the first shop tile while the other three arrive still woven and resolve in place → the canvas hands off to real `<img>` markup at the same measured rectangles.
- **The grid inherits the mechanism.** Every product picture arrives on the same loom (coarse cell → sharp, staggered), driven by an IntersectionObserver instead of scroll, so a **category filter change re-runs the weave** — the filter is felt as cloth being run off again, not a list swap.
- **Sections:** masthead (paper-on-ink over the scene, ink-on-paper past it, with its own scrim so nav stays legible over the weave) → scene → shop (filter + nine cards) → size & fit → care (dark band, rhyming with the scene's opening) → delivery & returns → reviews → the shop → footer. Bag is a right-hand drawer on desktop, a bottom sheet on touch.
- **Material:** all nine garments now exist. Five new cloths were synthesised at yarn level (white jersey, brushed charcoal wool, stone wool/cotton twill, chunky alpaca knit, khaki twill) and composited into flat-lay garments with grain direction, drape, seams, topstitch and hardware. Pipeline is in `tools/`.
- **Interaction baseline:** hover/focus-visible/press on every control; shuttle-fill on Add to bag; sold-out sizes struck and disabled; `aria-pressed` on sizes and filters; live regions for size state, filter count and bag sums; skip link; ESC + focus trap + focus restore on the bag; the unlanded scene row is `inert` so Tab never lands on invisible controls.

**Tested**

Desktop 1440, mobile 390, narrow 320 (no overflow). Normal motion: slow, fast, mid-scrub reversal and a full reverse to the top — the scene tracks, the handoff undoes cleanly. Reduced motion tested separately: no canvas, the scene resolves to a two-column held composition, images visible, transitions collapsed. Buying flow exercised end to end: size → add → bag count → drawer lines with name/size/price → remove → subtotal, £4.95 delivery and "£66.00 more for free delivery" under £100, free over it. Filter counts verified (All 9, Shirts 2, Outerwear 2, Trousers 3, Knitwear 2). Production build served and re-checked.

**Limitations**

The garment images are authored, not photographed — the page says so in the shop intro, under the scene row, and in the footer. Licensed photography wasn't a usable route here: Unsplash and Pexels blocked automated access, and the open-licence sources I could reach (Openverse, Met) had nothing coherent for a modern menswear label, so I made the cloth instead. The Shawl Cardigan's collar is the weakest silhouette of the nine. No WebGL2 falls back to the same still composition as reduced motion.

