The full route is built around the anchor. Nothing committed; `npm run build` succeeds.

## What shipped

**The anchor, untouched.** The loom scene still opens inside 12oz indigo canvas at yarn scale, pulls back as the weave cell falls from 30px to 1, draws an editorial frame around the Chore Jacket, holds it sharp beside its name and price, then hands the frame into the first tile of the shop while the rest of the row arrives still woven and closes up in place. Ground travels ink → paper across the same scroll.

**The route leads into and out of it with one grammar — cloth.**
- **Masthead** — paper-on-ink over the scene, ink-on-paper past it, with a bag count that bumps on add.
- **Shop** — all nine garments, category filter with counts and All, per-card detail/fabric/colours, size chips with sold-out sizes struck through and unaddable, size-before-add, live status line.
- **Size & fit / Care / Delivery / Reviews / The shop** — every required fact, laid out head-left / content-right so the closing sections share one rhythm; care inverts to ink as the page's second dark beat.
- **Bag** — drawer on desktop, bottom sheet on mobile; names each line's garment, size and price, removes lines, running subtotal, delivery threshold with the exact shortfall and a thread-coloured gauge to £100.

**Motion beyond the hero reuses the same renderer, not new tricks.** `WeaveGrid` runs the loom shader over the grid: each card's picture arrives woven and resolves where it sits, then hands off to the real `<img>`. Filtering re-weaves the new set, so the filter has a material response. Everything else is restraint: settle-in reveals, hairline underlines, press states.

## Tested
- Desktop 1440, mobile 390, narrow 320 (no horizontal overflow); normal motion and reduced motion separately.
- Reduced motion is authored, not degraded: a static editorial spread — garment, headline, honest copy, caption — with its own copy line, solid masthead, and no scrub.
- Bought end to end: choose size → add → bag → remove → threshold recalculates (£78 → "£22.00 more for free delivery"). Sold-out sizes are disabled. Tab order, focus rings, Escape-to-close, focus trap and restore all work.
- Scrub holds 60fps (median 16.7ms/frame) through the whole scene.

## Two things to know
- **Three real blockers came out of `dreative finalize` and are fixed**: the sticky filter bar rode over the cards it filtered (now in the flow), the stage's shop row sat behind the hero type before it was needed (now hidden until the handoff), and reveals resolved too late (now fire on a region's first pixel). Faded hero copy was also swallowing clicks on the landed row — fixed.
- **Finalization still fails on one check I can't honestly satisfy**: `missing verified install manifest at .claude/skills/dreative/.dreative-install.json`. No run in this testbed has that file; it's an installation artifact, not something the build produces, and I won't fabricate a verification record. Everything else passes — `npm run build`, `dreative docs-check`, and all visual-smoke checks at desktop, 390, 320 and reduced motion — so `DREATIVE_CHECKS_PASSED` was not printed.

Implementation complete; human taste verdict: awaiting user review.